WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.733
If a partition lives on one broker's disk, a dead disk loses its payments.

2
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:11.609
So Kafka keeps copies, called replicas, on three brokers.

3
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:13.557
One replica is the leader.

4
00:00:13.557 --> 00:00:17.933
Producers write only to it, and only the leader gives out offsets.

5
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:19.789
The other two are followers.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.122
A producer sends three payments.

7
00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:25.770
The leader appends them as offsets five, six and seven.

8
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.892
For now, they exist on one disk.

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:34.390
The followers copy the leader: each one fetches new records and appends them at the same offsets.

10
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.243
The leader tracks the replicas that keep up.

11
00:00:37.243 --> 00:00:39.837
These are its in-sync replicas, the ISR.

12
00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:41.588
Right now that's all three.

13
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.995
The high watermark marks how far every in-sync replica has copied.

14
00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:47.520
Here that's offset five.

15
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.207
Records below it are on all of them, so they're committed.

16
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:54.070
Consumers read only below the high watermark.

17
00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.527
They never see a payment that could vanish with the leader.

18
00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:59.887
Broker 2 fetches five to seven.

19
00:00:59.887 --> 00:01:03.638
Broker 3 is stuck on a stalled disk, and gets nothing.

20
00:01:03.638 --> 00:01:07.737
It's still in the ISR, so the high watermark stays at five.

21
00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.770
The producer set acks=all.

22
00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:16.151
It hears back only when the high watermark passes its records, so one slow disk holds it up.

23
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:21.449
After 30 seconds without catching up, the leader drops broker 3 from the ISR.

24
00:01:21.449 --> 00:01:25.937
The high watermark jumps to eight, and the producer gets its answer.

25
00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.065
Now broker 2 stops as well.

26
00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:34.393
The ISR is the leader alone, and the producer would be told a payment on one disk is safe.

27
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.812
min.insync.replicas sets a floor.

28
00:01:36.812 --> 00:01:44.853
At two, the leader refuses new payments with NOT_ENOUGH_REPLICAS, and the producer keeps retrying for up to two minutes.

29
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:49.988
So acks=all waits for the ISR, and the floor keeps that ISR big enough.

30
00:01:49.988 --> 00:01:53.592
Every acknowledged payment is on at least two disks.
